// === ESP32-S3-EYE blob tracker — class-based, S42-fix version ===
//
// This is the post-S42 ship-ready eye_demo.  Pre-S42, method-call sites
// like `List.new(Color.new().init(...), ...)` silently elided the outer
// call (the inner Color.new returned, but the outer List.new dropped its
// args and returned the last Color instead of a List wrapping them).
// Workaround was flat parallel lists; with S42 fixed (vm: introduce
// OP_SELF for method-call dispatch) the natural class-based idiom
// works.  See REVIVAL.md §14 / docs/urbi-embedded-design-risks.md.
//
// Reactive runtime exercised:
//   * Two chained at(blob_seen?) handlers (crosshair update + counter)
//   * Three chained at(button_pressed?) handlers (advance + apply + log)
//   * Class instances carry the per-colour palette state; method calls
//     on the list (`.get(i)`) and on the instances (`.r`, `.g`, etc.)
//     run through the new OP_SELF + method-flagged OP_CALL path.
//
// v0.7.x lex/emit guardrails still in effect:
//   * No `[...]` list literal — use List.new(...).
//   * No `&&`/`||` shortcut — nested `if`.
//   * No `%` modulo — wrap table via List.new(1, 2, 0).
//   * Async at-bodies stay single-statement; function-bodied at-handlers
//     remain on the design-risks list (S43, separate from S42).
//   * Chained handlers (multiple `at (e?)` on the same event) run in
//     install order since the v0.7.2 pending-refire counter widening.

// === Color palette ======================================================
//
// Color packages RGB target + tolerance + name.  `init` returns `this`
// so the call chains: Color.new().init(...) yields a fully-populated
// instance suitable for List.new().
//
// Targets pulled off pure-saturated corners because real RGB565 of
// "red/green/blue" objects shows ~5-15 units of sensor noise + AWB
// leak on the "should be zero" channels.  Pure (31,0,0)/tol=4 matches
// almost nothing on a live feed; the wider centres catch most real
// objects under typical lighting.
class Color {
    var init = function (r, g, b, tol, name) {
        this.r = r; this.g = g; this.b = b;
        this.tol = tol;
        this.name = name;
        this
    }
};

// S42 exercise: inline nested calls (List.new(Color.new().init(...), ...))
// must now wrap each Color instance correctly into a List.
Realm.colors = List.new(
    Color.new().init(24,  6,  6, 12, "RED"),
    Color.new().init( 6, 48,  6, 16, "GREEN"),
    Color.new().init( 6,  6, 24, 12, "BLUE"));

// Wrap table: index N maps to (N+1) mod 3.  Pure-urbiscript state
// machine since `%` doesn't exist at v1.0.
Realm.idx      = 0;
Realm.next_idx = List.new(1, 2, 0);

// Counter incremented on every blob_seen event.  Read by the button
// log handler so each press dumps "total blobs: N" — at-a-glance
// signal that blob detection is still running between presses.
Realm.blob_count = 0;

log("eye_demo (class-based, S42-fix) loaded - BOOT cycles RED -> GREEN -> BLUE");

// === BLOB SEEN — two chained at-handlers ================================
//
// destructure_blob (eye_demo_main.c) runs on the urbi task at safepoint
// drain and writes the centroid into Realm.last_blob_x / _y / _area.
// These two at-handlers fire in install order on each blob event.
//
// Two strand spawns per blob event × 25 Hz camera = 50 strand spawns/sec.
// Per spawn the body runs ~5-10 bytecode dispatch ops.  Light load.
at (blob_seen?) draw_crosshair(Realm.last_blob_x, Realm.last_blob_y);
at (blob_seen?) Realm.blob_count = Realm.blob_count + 1;

// === BUTTON CYCLE — three chained at-handlers ===========================
//
// Pure-urbiscript state machine, S42 fix actively exercised:
//
//   1. Advance the wrap-table index (modulo 3 via next_idx).
//   2. Push the new colour through set_target_color — host fn touches
//      the camera task's critical section under portMUX.  The arg
//      list reads Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).r / .g / .b / .tol —
//      method-call chains that pre-S42 would silently corrupt the
//      outer set_target_color call when intervening GETSLOTs clobbered
//      vm->last_recv during arg evaluation.
//   3. Log the new colour name + total blob count for visibility.
at (button_pressed?) Realm.idx = Realm.next_idx.get(Realm.idx);
at (button_pressed?) set_target_color(
    Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).r,
    Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).g,
    Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).b,
    Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).tol);
at (button_pressed?) log("target =>",
    Realm.colors.get(Realm.idx).name,
    "total blobs:",
    Realm.blob_count);
